Q: Exception when loading F# types that implement an interface which uses generics from an assembly A: <p>I am not sure if you are showing the code where the exception actually occurs, but I guess you are not looking for the correct method / property. Here is what works for me.</p>
<pre><code>match LoadPlugin &quot;Plugins/TestPlugin/TestPlugin.dll&quot; with
| None -&gt; ()
| Some p -&gt;
    let pluginType = p.GetType &quot;MyPlugin.SomePlugin&quot;
    let interfaceType = pluginType.GetInterface &quot;IPlugin&quot;
    let ctor = pluginType.GetConstructor [||]
    let pobj = ctor.Invoke [||]
    let prop = interfaceType.GetProperty &quot;TestString&quot;
    let propVal = prop.GetValue pobj
    printfn $&quot;propVal = {propVal}&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>If the exception is actually from the GetTypes() call, then I guess there is some problem with your setup. I would first try to empty the bin and obj folders.</p>
